        <mxCell id="panel_events" value="FIVE NON-STATE-CHANGING EVENTS (DOCS SEC 3.2)&#10;&#10;These events record operational milestones and corrections with date, time, and responsible,&#10;but do not alter the lifecycle state of the sack:&#10;&#10;1. arrived_at_center:&#10;   Transporter arrives at collection center yard and initiates physical handover.&#10;   Records recorded_at on transporter phone and links open trip to center gate arrival (A10 sec 7).&#10;&#10;2. assigned_to_trip:&#10;   Collection-center operator stages accepted sacks onto an outbound center_to_port trip.&#10;   Required guard condition before departed_to_port can be executed by transporter.&#10;&#10;3. code_replaced:&#10;   A damaged or illegible physical label is replaced with a fresh code from the center reserve.&#10;   The retired code is marked void in sack_codes and permanently returns 'not found' at lookup.&#10;&#10;4. weight_corrected:&#10;   Compensating event correcting scale typographical error. Must be recorded by the same role&#10;   and scope that entered original, citing mandatory reason (ASM-151). Retains full audit history.&#10;&#10;5. outcome_corrected:&#10;   Compensating event correcting reception outcome error (e.g. misclassified rejection).&#10;   Same role, scope, and reason rule applies (ASM-151).&#10;&#10;Append-Only Immutability Contract:&#10;Zero events are edited or deleted. Every physical act is persisted immutably in sack_event_log.&#10;State is derived by replaying history." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#94a3b8;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#1e293b;fontSize=13.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="890" width="1040" height="680" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="panel_rules" value="OFFLINE ORDERING &amp; TIMESTAMP RECONCILIATION (ASM-152, SEC 3.3, SEC 4)&#10;&#10;Every mobile and field actor operates offline on mountain roads. Events reach AWS out of sequence.&#10;Four deterministic rules govern state resolution:&#10;&#10;Rule 1: Refuse Only What Caller Cannot Do&#10;   API rejects requests only for invalid credentials/role, unknown/void code, or schema invalidity.&#10;   Once an event represents a physical act that already occurred, it is unconditionally persisted.&#10;&#10;Rule 2: Order by Time of the Act (Deterministic Fold)&#10;   Current sack state is recomputed from scratch by replaying the complete event log ordered strictly&#10;   by recorded_at ASC, then event_id ASC. Result is mathematically invariant to network arrival order!&#10;&#10;Rule 3: Physical Receiver is Authoritative&#10;   A custody transition recorded by the physical holder (T3, T4, T7, T8) is applied immediately even if&#10;   upstream departure or pickup is still queued in a disconnected phone buffer. Missing steps flagged.&#10;&#10;Rule 4: Pre-Registration Events Wait in Pending State&#10;   An event arriving for an issued code prior to its sack_registered upload is held in pending status&#10;   and applied automatically when the registration drains from the farmer's outbox.&#10;&#10;Timestamp Rules (Sec 4):&#10;• recorded_at: Device UTC timestamp to millisecond taken at moment of physical act.&#10;  Formatted in America/Bogota (UTC-5) for display (ASM-007).&#10;• received_at: Server UTC timestamp applied by API upon durable persistence in DynamoDB.&#10;• Clock Skew Check: If recorded_at &gt; received_at + 5 min, flagged as phone clock ahead (PD-151)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#94a3b8;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#1e293b;fontSize=13.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1110" y="890" width="1080" height="680" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="panel_stores" value="DATA SCHEMA &amp; STORE ARCHITECTURE (DOCS SEC 4, SEC 10) [BOX D04, D06]&#10;&#10;Mandatory Event Record Schema (Sec 4):&#10;• event_id: UUID idempotency key generated on device (A10 sec 2)&#10;• event_type: Transition event or non-state-changing event type&#10;• sack_codes: List of Crockford Base32 sack codes covered in batch act&#10;• trip_id: Trip reference (empty for sack_registered)&#10;• recorded_at / received_at: Device act timestamp / API persistence time&#10;• responsible_subject_id / role: Opaque pseudonym &amp; Cognito role (ASM-091)&#10;• device_id / center_id: App installation UUID &amp; collection center ID&#10;• latitude / longitude: GNSS fix coordinates for transporter custody acts&#10;• weight_kg / drying_lot_id: Measured weight &amp; drying lot identifier&#10;• outcome / reason / receiver_reference: Status, rationale, port receipt ref&#10;&#10;DynamoDB Store Topology (On-Demand Mode, KMS Customer Keys):&#10;• sack_event_log: PK event_id | Immutable event log | KMS 'records' | Streams enabled&#10;• sacks: PK sack_id | GSI sack_code, farm_id | Current state, version, flags | KMS 'records'&#10;• sack_history: PK sack_id, SK recorded_at#event_id | Deterministic fold source | KMS 'records'&#10;• trips: PK trip_id | Transporter custody legs &amp; vehicles | KMS 'records'&#10;• transport_positions: PK trip_id, SK sequence_no | 5-min GNSS fixes | KMS 'telemetry' (PD-110)&#10;• buyer_view: PK sack_code | Projected public view | KMS 'public_view' (ASM-154)&#10;&#10;Disaster Recovery Objectives (Sec 9, ASM-157, PD-153):&#10;• RPO = 15 min: sack-exporter streams JSON Lines to S3 export prefix (ADR-001) every 60 s;&#10;  CloudWatch alarm fires if iterator age &gt; 5 min.&#10;• RTO = 4 h: Public lookup runs serverless via CloudFront + Lambda URL + buyer_view;&#10;  completely decoupled from application API!" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#94a3b8;strokeWidth=2;fontColor=#1e293b;fontSize=13.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=14;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2220" y="890" width="1120" height="680" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>